WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.592
NumPy is often working behind the scenes in data analysis and machine learning.

00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:12.067
Analysts may use it together with Pandas, SQL, and Jupiter notebooks.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:20.379
Data scientists often use it with Pandas, scikit-learn, statistical methods, and machine learning models.

00:00:20.829 --> 00:00:24.561
The practical skill is understanding numerical arrays.

00:00:24.561 --> 00:00:32.166
Imagine that you have thousands of sales values, temperatures, sensor readings, or model features.

00:00:32.166 --> 00:00:37.161
You usually do not want to write a Python loop for every calculation.

00:00:37.161 --> 00:00:42.691
NumPy lets you apply one operation to many values at the same time.

00:00:42.691 --> 00:00:48.346
That makes the code shorter, easier to read, and often much faster.

00:00:48.346 --> 00:00:55.816
When you later work with machine learning, you will see the same idea because models typically expect numerical data

00:00:55.816 --> 00:00:58.492
organized as vectors or matrices.
